// fake.nv — the locale, and the three calls that turn a generator into
// values.
//
// A FAKE IS A STRATEGY.  Not a wrapper around one, not a thing that can
// be converted into one: `fakename.first_name(FakeEn)` answers a
// `PropStrategy<Str>`, which is proptest-core-nv's own type, and every
// combinator in that package works on it.  A fixture and a property test
// therefore draw from one source, and a suite that wants "a hundred
// plausible customers, and also the property that the importer never
// loses one" writes one generator and uses it twice.
//
// WHY THAT, AND NOT A GENERATOR TYPE OF OUR OWN.  Three reasons, and the
// first is not a preference:
//
//   1. **The layer decided it.**  A `core` package may depend only on
//      `core` packages.  rand-nv is `host` — it declares `[fs, rand]`,
//      because half of it is the operating system's CSPRNG — so the
//      plan's other option, "a function of a rand-nv state", is not
//      reachable from this layer at all.  proptest-core-nv is `core`,
//      and its `Tape` is a seeded splitmix64 with no effect in it.
//   2. **A second generator type would be a second ecosystem.**
//      `strategy.list_of`, `strategy.option_of`, `strategy.map` and
//      `strategy.one_of` are exactly the combinators a fixture wants —
//      twenty of these, optionally absent, mapped into a caller's own
//      struct — and reimplementing them here would be a hundred
//      functions that do the same thing under different names.
//   3. **One transcript.**  A failure in a property test that used a
//      fake reproduces from the tape, and the tape does not know or care
//      which of its draws were "fake" and which were "property".
//
// DOES A FAKE SHRINK?  The question the row on the grid asks, and the
// answer is YES, which is not the obvious one.  Shrinking in
// proptest-core-nv is arithmetic on the CHOICE SEQUENCE and not on the
// value, so anything that draws through the tape shrinks for free — a
// name drawn as an index into a table shrinks towards index 0, which is
// the first name in the table.
//
// What a fake does not do is shrink *meaningfully in its domain*:
// "Zdenka Sørensen" shrinking to "Aaron" is arithmetic and not
// simplification a reader would have chosen.  In practice that is fine
// and occasionally better than fine — a counterexample reported with the
// first name in the table is a counterexample whose name is not the
// point, which is usually exactly true.  A test that wants a specific
// shrink writes `strategy.just`.
//
// THE SEED IS THE WHOLE CONTRACT.  Every generator is a pure function of
// the tape it is handed, so `fake.one(g, 42)` is the same value on every
// machine, every run, every toolchain that agrees on `tape.split_step`.
// `fake.seed_line` is the line a failing test should print, and it is
// the line a person pastes back.
//
// THE LOCALE IS A VALUE THE CALLER PASSES, never a global and never a
// default.  A library with a global locale is a library where one test
// changes another's data, and a default locale is a library that makes
// English the unmarked case — which is wrong for this project and wrong
// for the first Danish consumer.  Every generator that could differ by
// locale takes one.

use strategy
use tape

// Which locale a generator draws from.
//
// Two shipped, and the pair is deliberate rather than a start: one
// locale is a library that cannot be tested for locale-dependence at
// all, and two is the smallest number that proves the seam.  `en` and
// `da` because this project's first consumers are in both, and because
// Danish exercises the parts an English-only fake never does — `æ`, `ø`
// and `å` in a name, a postcode that is four digits and not five, a
// phone number that is eight digits with no area code, and a street
// name that comes before its number.
//
// A third locale is a table and no new code, which is the point of the
// value being a parameter.
//
// ```novo
// use fake
//
// fn main() [io]
//     println(fake.locale_name(FakeDa))                     // da
// ```
pub enum FakeLocale
    // English, as spoken in the United States: five-digit postcodes,
    // a number before the street name, a ten-digit telephone number.
    FakeEn
    // Danish: four-digit postcodes, the number after the street name,
    // an eight-digit telephone number with no area code, and names
    // that contain characters an ASCII-only fixture never produces.
    FakeDa

// The locale's BCP 47 tag.
//
// `en` and `da`, which is what a caller writing the seed and the locale
// into a failure report wants, and what a caller reading one back
// parses.
//
// ```novo
// use fake
//
// fn main() [io]
//     println(fake.locale_name(FakeEn))                     // en
// ```
pub fn locale_name(loc: FakeLocale) -> Str
    todo("fake-nv.fake.locale_name")

// The locale a tag names, or `None` for one this package does not ship.
//
// For a caller taking the locale from a configuration file or a command
// line.  `None` rather than a silent fall back to English: a test that
// asked for `de` and got American addresses is a test whose failure
// nobody can explain.
//
// ```novo
// use fake
//
// fn main() [io]
//     match fake.locale_of("de")
//         Some(_) => println("shipped")
//         None    => println("not shipped")                 // this one
// ```
pub fn locale_of(tag: Str) -> ?FakeLocale
    todo("fake-nv.fake.locale_of")

// Every locale this package ships.
//
// A list rather than a comment, because a test that wants to run its
// fixtures under all of them loops over this and keeps working when a
// third arrives.
//
// ```novo
// use fake
// use std.list
//
// fn main() [io]
//     println("${list.len(fake.locales())}")                // 2
// ```
pub fn locales() -> [FakeLocale]
    todo("fake-nv.fake.locales")

// **One value from a generator and a seed.**
//
// The call a fixture makes.  The same seed gives the same value on every
// machine and every run, which is the whole contract: a test that fails
// on seed 42 fails on seed 42 tomorrow, on somebody else's laptop, on
// the build machine.
//
// ```novo
// use fake
// use fakename
//
// fn main() [io]
//     println(fake.one(fakename.first_name(FakeEn), 42))
// ```
pub fn one<T>(g: PropStrategy<T>, seed: Int) -> T
    todo("fake-nv.fake.one")

// `n` values from a generator and a seed.
//
// Drawn from ONE tape in sequence, so the values differ from each other
// — which is what a caller seeding a database wants and what `n` calls
// to `one` with the same seed would not give.  A caller that wants `n`
// copies of one value wants `list.repeat`.
//
// ```novo
// use fake
// use fakename
// use std.list
//
// fn main() [io]
//     let names = fake.many(fakename.first_name(FakeEn), 42, 10)
//     println("${list.len(names)}")                         // 10
// ```
pub fn many<T>(g: PropStrategy<T>, seed: Int, n: Int) -> [T]
    todo("fake-nv.fake.many")

// A value and the tape that follows it.
//
// The composing form: for a caller drawing several different generators
// from one seed, where each draw has to continue where the last one
// stopped.  `one` and `many` are this with the tape made and dropped
// inside.
//
// ```novo
// use fake
// use fakename
// use fakeplace
// use tape
//
// fn main() [io]
//     let t0 = tape.from_seed(42)
//     let (name, t1) = fake.draw(fakename.full_name(FakeDa), t0)
//     let (city, t2) = fake.draw(fakeplace.city(FakeDa), t1)
//     println("${name} — ${city}")
// ```
pub fn draw<T>(g: PropStrategy<T>, t: Tape) -> (T, Tape)
    todo("fake-nv.fake.draw")

// The line a failing test should print.
//
// `fake seed: 42 (en)` — the seed and the locale, which together are
// everything needed to reproduce the data.  One line, one shape, so a
// person reading a build log recognises it and a script can find it.
//
// It exists rather than being left to each caller because the value of a
// reproducible fixture is entirely in somebody actually printing the
// seed, and a library that only made it possible would find that most
// suites did not.
//
// ```novo
// use fake
//
// fn main() [io]
//     println(fake.seed_line(42, FakeEn))                   // fake seed: 42 (en)
// ```
pub fn seed_line(seed: Int, loc: FakeLocale) -> Str
    todo("fake-nv.fake.seed_line")

// The seed and locale a `seed_line` carried, or `None`.
//
// The other half: a person pastes the line from a build log into a test
// and gets the run back.  `None` for a line that is not one, so a caller
// reading a log file can skip everything else.
//
// ```novo
// use fake
//
// fn main() [io]
//     match fake.parse_seed_line("fake seed: 42 (en)")
//         Some(_) => println("reproducible")                // this one
//         None    => println("not a seed line")
// ```
pub fn parse_seed_line(line: Str) -> ?(Int, FakeLocale)
    todo("fake-nv.fake.parse_seed_line")
